{
  "origin": "Planning's second tier had no coverage, and it is the tier the programme was opened for: a product decision made in planning has nowhere to land, because a corrigendum carries what the record determined and never a decision nobody made. Its home is the discussion, and the specification re-aligns to it. This walks a defect the record leaves open — what the shopper is shown while a capture is unconfirmed — through the brief exchange, the landing in the discussion in that document's own idiom, the corrigendum citing it, and the amended task list the user then approves. Its twin, planning-routes-a-gap-and-pauses, meets the same raise with a user who says it needs real discussion work.",
